    IN CONNECTION WITH THE USE OR PERFORMANCE OF THIS SOFTWARE.

  The test data in internal/cli/testdata and the keys checked in
  internal/ledger/ledgersim come from cardano-hw-cli's Ledger integration
  tests, under the same license.

- internal/ledger is ported from ledgerjs-hw-app-cardano by Vacuumlabs,
  now kept by the Cardano Foundation
  (https://github.com/cardano-foundation/ledgerjs-hw-app-cardano),
  licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

- internal/cli/argparse.go and internal/cli/helpformat.go reproduce, in
  Go, the parsing algorithm and the help formatting of the argparse
  package for JavaScript (https://github.com/nodeca/argparse) version
  2.0.1, itself a port of Python 3.9's argparse module:

    Copyright (C) 2010-2020 Python Software Foundation.
    Copyright (C) 2020 argparse.js authors

  licensed under the Python Software Foundation License Version 2, whose
  text is in LICENSE-PSF. Summary of the changes: only the parts that
  cardano-hw-cli's command line uses are reproduced (subcommands, long
  options with one, an optional or no value, repeatable options, mutually
  exclusive groups, prefixes of options, type functions, help and usage
  formatting, and the line wrapping of the JavaScript port), rewritten in
  Go with the command tree of cardano-hw-cli.

The Trezor Host Protocol (internal/trezor/thp) is implemented from its
published specification. The Trezor protocol buffers messages
(internal/trezor/msg) are written by hand from the message layouts that
SatoshiLabs defines in trezor-firmware (LGPL-3.0); no file of that project
is included.
